Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Show images inside a line of text on iOS

Images that share a line with text or other markup (README badges,
[![badge](...)](...), an <img> inside <a> or <p>) could not be block
fragments, so they rendered as alt text or inert HTML source. The iOS
reader now passes an InlineImageContext to PresentationMaps, and
InlineImageDisplay replaces each such image's source span with an
attachment, the way inline math is drawn. The source is untouched; alt
text stands in until a picture loads or if it never does; an image inside
a link keeps the link. Arrivals coalesce into one rebuild that keeps the
scroll position, and a column change refits the pictures.

The Mac passes no context, so its rendering is unchanged. Also marks
RemoteImageLoader.maximumBytes nonisolated (a Swift 6 warning).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
