@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ This file contains Downright-specific context, invariants, and evidence gates. F
 
 - For code changes, use focused tests while iterating, then run `Scripts/check.sh` as the authoritative source gate. For documentation-only changes, inspect content, links, and referenced commands without rebuilding the app. Do not substitute bare `swift test`; zero executed tests or a masked pipeline failure is a failed gate.
 - When a change touches `MarkdownCore` or the shared (non-`View/`) half of `MarkdownRender`, also run `Scripts/check-ios.sh`. It requires Xcode and builds for iOS devices and the simulator. It also generates and tests the read-only iOS app in `iOSApp/` when XcodeGen is installed. It does not replace `Scripts/check.sh`. The iOS app is not a release surface: nothing in `Docs/RELEASE.md` covers it. Shared code names platform types through `MarkdownRender/Platform/Platform.swift`, not `NSColor`/`NSFont`/`NSImage` directly.
-- Remote images: `MarkdownCore` and `MarkdownRender` never make network requests. `https:` images render only through a `RemoteImageLoading` a host installs on its view; the Mac app and Quick Look never install one, so there they stay blocked or inert. The iOS app installs its loader while Settings › Apps › Downright › Load Remote Images is on (the default): cookie-free, size- and time-limited fetches, with SVG drawn in an off-screen, script-free WebKit view.
+- Remote images: `MarkdownCore` and `MarkdownRender` never make network requests. `https:` images render only through a `RemoteImageLoading` a host installs on its view; the Mac app and Quick Look never install one, so there they stay blocked or inert. The iOS app installs its loader while Settings › Apps › Downright › Load Remote Images is on (the default): cookie-free, size- and time-limited fetches, with SVG drawn by a hidden, script-free WebKit view. Images inside a line of text (badges, `[![…](…)](…)`) are presented only by the iOS reader, through `InlineImageDisplay`'s display substitutions; the Mac passes no inline image context, so its rendering of them is unchanged.
 - Give concurrent checks unique scratch/build locations using the supported variables: `SCRATCH`, `TEST_SCRATCH`, `APP_ACCEPTANCE_SCRATCH`, `SPOTLIGHT_SCRATCH`, and `IOS_SCRATCH` (for `Scripts/check-ios.sh`). Release benchmarks default to `${SCRATCH}-bench`; `BENCH_SCRATCH` can override that location. If source, `HEAD`, or relevant outputs change during validation, discard the result and rerun on the intended snapshot.
 - `Scripts/bundle-app.sh` is appropriate for host-only iteration but does not prove Finder extensions. Use `Scripts/bundle-xcode-app.sh` and `Scripts/check-app.sh` for Quick Look, thumbnails, Finder integration, or production-shaped app acceptance. Development/ad-hoc bundles do not prove production Sparkle behavior. Every nested Mach-O must support all architectures of its host; universal release archives must include Intel and Apple Silicon CLI and Spotlight binaries.
 - When the installed app is the acceptance surface, install the intended artifact explicitly with `APP_SOURCE=... Scripts/install.sh`, stop stale Downright instances when safe, and verify bundle path, version/build, executable identity, signature, embedded components, and running process before exercising the feature.
